        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "***EXCELLENT CENTRAL LOCATION / OWN DOOR ACCESS / WHEELCHAIR ACCESSIBLE / NO RENTAL CAPS***\r\n\r\nKELLY BRADSHAW are delighted to introduce 67 The Old Distillery, Beresford Street, Smithfield, Dublin 7.\r\n \r\nLong before No. 67 became a city home, this part of Dublin was a place of brewing, distilling and industry. A small brewery was established on the site as far back as the early eighteenth century, before the premises evolved into a much larger distillery through the coming together of the Jameson and Pim families. \r\n\r\nThe site expanded significantly during the nineteenth century, with the construction of the impressive granite malthouse which remains such an important part of The Old Distillery's character today. No. 67 offers the opportunity to become part of the story, with this appealing ground floor one-bedroom apartment perfectly positioned for enjoying everything Dublin 7 has to offer.\r\n\r\nInside, the accommodation is wonderfully straightforward and easy to live in. The entrance hall leads through to a generous open-plan kitchen, living and dining room, creating a natural heart to the home. The generous proportions allow the space to work equally well for relaxing at the end of the day, enjoying dinner with friends or simply having somewhere comfortable to unwind. The room's shape also gives it a little more character than the standard open-plan apartment, while the separate bedroom provides a peaceful space away from the main living area.\r\n\r\nThe bathroom is conveniently positioned off the entrance hall, and the overall layout makes excellent use of the available space. It’s practical without compromising on comfort, and particularly well suited to anyone looking for a manageable city base without sacrificing the feeling of having a proper home.\r\n\r\nLife at The Old Distillery puts you right in the middle of one of Dublin's most exciting and established neighbourhoods. Smithfield is quite literally on the doorstep, with its cafés, restaurants, bars and cultural attractions, while Stoneybatter, Capel Street and the city centre are all within easy reach. \r\n\r\nThe Luas is close by, making getting across the city wonderfully convenient, while the Four Courts, the River Liffey and Phoenix Park are also readily accessible. The location of No.67 allows you to leave the car behind and genuinely enjoy the city on foot. Morning coffee, dinner with friends, a walk through the Phoenix Park or an evening in the city can all become part of everyday life, rather than something that requires planning.\r\n\r\nFor first-time buyers, those looking for a city base, or an investor seeking a property in a well-established Dublin 7 development, No. 67 offers an appealing combination of history, character, convenience and modern city living.\r\n\r\nThere is a lovely sense of continuity here. A site that has been part of Dublin's working history for centuries has been given a completely new purpose, and No. 67 is now ready for its next chapter."
